<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Compaq estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Compaq estimates raised.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robertson Stephens &amp; Co analyst Dan Niles raised his earnings forecasts for Compaq Computer Corp following its report Thursday of strong second quarter earnings.</p>
<p>-- Niles raised his 1997 forecast to $6.50 a share from $6.40 and 1998 to $8.00 a share from $7.70.</p>
<p>-- In a statement, he noted Compaq's gross margin sequentially increased 80 basis points due to a richer product mix, improved cost efficiencies and a restructured distribution channel.</p>
<p>-- Compaq shares were up 4-5/16 at 124-5/8.</p>
</text>
